From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Retain Theora pixel aspect from the Ogg identification header

The header probe consumed but discarded Theora's aspect numerator and
denominator. A decoder relying on the demux format then produced square
pixels even when the source declared non-square pixels. Keep both fields
in the elementary stream format so the first output has the declared SAR.
---
diff --git a/modules/demux/ogg.c b/modules/demux/ogg.c
--- a/modules/demux/ogg.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ogg.c
@@ -2682,8 +2682,8 @@ static bool Ogg_ReadTheoraHeader( logical_stream_t *p_stream,
     i_fps_numerator = bs_read( &bitstream, 32 );
     i_fps_denominator = bs_read( &bitstream, 32 );
     i_fps_denominator = __MAX( i_fps_denominator, 1 );
-    bs_read( &bitstream, 24 ); /* aspect_numerator */
-    bs_read( &bitstream, 24 ); /* aspect_denominator */
+    p_stream->fmt.video.i_sar_num = bs_read( &bitstream, 24 );
+    p_stream->fmt.video.i_sar_den = bs_read( &bitstream, 24 );
 
     p_stream->fmt.video.i_frame_rate = i_fps_numerator;
     p_stream->fmt.video.i_frame_rate_base = i_fps_denominator;
